@spec vm_retune_spec  src=tests/specs/vm_retune_spec.lua  loc=508  cases=23
@exercises tuning (tuning), trackerView (h.vm), editCursor (h.ec), configManager (h.cm), trackerManager (h.tm)
@surface   tuning.derive, tuning.genDiamond, vm:setGridSize, tuning.stepToMidi, tuning.scalaPitch, vm:retune, ec:setSelection, cm:set, cm:getAt, tm:addEvent, tm:flush
@harness   mk{seed.notes}

# Intent
  Retune: with no target tv:retune(slots) runs every note in scope through
  tuning.snap and writes the pair back, strength being how far of the way there
  it actually lands, and remembers the target and key on the take. The notation
  is a twelve-note quarter-comma meantone MOS, so a step's seat carries a detune
  of its own and the window is asymmetric (+38.0 / -58.6 either side of step 1).
  
  With a target it is the solve: the scope's notes grouped into strands by
  step-class, shortlisted from the notation and the target, and handed to
  sonority.solveToPoints. Those cases write a dominant seventh under a 12-EDO notation
  against the 7-limit diamond at odd limit 9 -- the chord the pull is calibrated
  on (design/adaptive-tuning.md § Harmonic lock) -- and a tritone against the
  5-limit diamond at odd limit 15, the hole that refuses a solve.
  
  With the facility on 'moves' the same target is read as intervals rather than
  points: sonority.solveToMoves spells the strands against one another and settles
  them by springs. Those cases write a C major and a C minor triad against 1/1, 5/4
  and 3/2, the minor third being what no point of it reaches, and the purity slot
  is what the springs hold their intervals to.
  
  Either facility reads a note's render clip rather than its authored ceiling, so an
  open tail sounds to the next onset in its lane rather than to the end of the take.
  
  A note carrying an intent is stranded and seated on the step that intent names rather
  than on the step its pitch reads as (design/sounding-anchor.md § What the note remembers).

# Helpers
  @fn mk(harness, notes, temper, tempers)  @ 48-56
  @fn note(ppq, pitch, detune, intentCents)  @ 58-61
  @fn lane1(h)  @ 63-67
  @fn cell(h, row)  @ 69
  @fn near(a, b, msg)  @ 71-73
  @fn settles(a, b, msg)  @ 77-79
      -- The springs answer by relaxation rather than by construction, so their placements are
      -- pinned to the thousandth of a cent the sweep converges to.
  @fn seat(step, oct)  @ 82
      -- Seat of (step, octave) under MEAN, as the spec's expectation frame.
  @fn c7()  @ 85-87
      -- The C7 the pull is calibrated on, written at 12-EDO.
  @fn cellsAt(h, row)  @ 90-97
      -- The chord at a row, as cells by the pitch they sound on: every chan-1 note lane at once.
  @fn chordAt(h, row)  @ 100-104
      -- The same chord as detune alone, which is what most of these cases read.
  @fn offset(token, semitones)  @ 107
      -- The detune a target point lands as, seated on the 12-EDO note it is written on.

# Cases
  @case 'retune(all) seats an off-step note on its own step'  [harness]  @ 111-120
  @case 'a note past the half-way point lands on its neighbour'  [harness]  @ 124-133
  @case 'a note inside the window keeps its step'  [harness]  @ 137-144
  @case 'a note already on its step is left where it is'  [harness]  @ 148-156
  @case 'the snap seats a note on the step its intent names, and spends the intent'  [harness]  @ 160-174
  @case 'a selection confines the snap to the notes inside it'  [harness]  @ 178-187
  @case 'half strength closes half the distance, and again on the next run'  [harness]  @ 191-201
  @case 'a blend below full strength is re-seated on the nearest semitone'  [harness]  @ 205-215
  @case 'zero strength moves nothing, not even the written pitch'  [harness]  @ 219-227
  @case 'retune remembers the target and the key on the take'  [harness]  @ 231-245
  @case 'retune with no target forgets the one the take carried'  [harness]  @ 249-255
  @case 'a dominant seventh takes the otonal seventh the diamond offers'  [harness]  @ 259-269
  @case 'above the crossing the seventh gives up the otonal tuning'  [harness]  @ 273-281
  @case 'an octave doubling is seated in its own register, and moves no answer'  [harness]  @ 285-295
  @case 'a note moved off its step strands with the class its intent names'  [harness]  @ 299-312
  @case 'a step the target leaves nowhere to go refuses the solve and names it'  [harness]  @ 316-324
  @case 'widened, the refusing class takes the point the music around it wants'  [harness]  @ 328-347
  @case 'a widened solve stamps the step it carried a note off, and answers alike again'  [harness]  @ 351-370
  @case 'the facility decides how the same target is read'  [harness]  @ 374-396
  @case 'the moves facility spells a third the target holds no point for'  [harness]  @ 400-423
  @case 'purity prices how nearly the spelled intervals sound pure'  [harness]  @ 427-449
  @case 'a strand pinned to its window edge keeps the step it was written on'  [harness]  @ 453-476
  @case 'an open tail sounds to its clip, so a class returning is a second strand'  [harness]  @ 480-506

